    "grammar": [
      {
        "title": "Question words",
        "explanation_ar": "كلمات السؤال تأتي في بداية السؤال: what (ماذا) للأشياء، who (مَن) للأشخاص، where (أين) للمكان، when (متى) للزمن، why (لماذا) للسبب، how (كيف) للطريقة، which (أيّ) للاختيار.",
        "explanation_en": "Question words start a question: what (thing), who (person), where (place), when (time), why (reason), how (way), which (choice).",
        "examples": [
          "Where did you put the keys?",
          "When do you wake up?",
          "Which one do you want?"
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Modal verbs: can, will, should, may, would",
        "explanation_ar": "الأفعال المساعدة الناقصة يأتي بعدها الفعل في صورته الأساسية بدون to وبدون s: can (يستطيع)، will (سوف)، should (ينبغي)، may (قد)، would (للتأدب).",
        "explanation_en": "Modal verbs are followed by the base verb, with no \"to\" and no -s: can (ability), will (future), should (advice), may (possibility), would (polite).",
        "examples": [
          "Adam can fix the computer.",
          "You should visit the doctor.",
          "It may rain today."
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Comparatives with than",
        "explanation_ar": "للمقارنة بين شيئين نضيف er للصفة القصيرة ثم than: tall → taller than. ومع الصفات الطويلة نستخدم more: more valuable than.",
        "explanation_en": "To compare two things, add -er to a short adjective and use \"than\": taller than. With long adjectives use \"more\": more valuable than.",
        "examples": [
          "Zain is taller than Adam.",
          "This ring is more valuable than that one."
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Adverbs of frequency",
        "explanation_ar": "كلمات التكرار مثل always (دائماً)، sometimes (أحياناً)، never (أبداً) تأتي قبل الفعل الأساسي وبعد فعل be.",
        "explanation_en": "Frequency words like always, sometimes, never go before the main verb and after the verb \"be\".",
        "examples": [
          "I always go to work by car.",
          "We have never been to Australia.",
          "She is always on time."
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
